Appendix G: Rule-of-Three Reporting Template

For $n$ null-rebuild cycles with zero observed violations, the upper 95% bound on the per-cycle failure probability is approximately $3/n$. The benchmark report must state:

· $n$, the number of cycles;
· the environment set $\Gamma$ and the variation across it;
· the rule-of-three bound $3/n$;
· the observed hashes per environment;
· any cycle in which the flagged set changed even if the hash did not.

A report that states “deterministic across 100 cycles” without the bound is overclaiming: 100 cycles with zero failures is consistent with a per-cycle failure rate as high as roughly 3% at 95% confidence. The correct statement is “no failures in 100 cycles, with an upper 95% bound of 3% per cycle under the rule of three,” and the benchmark’s acceptance criterion should be stated in those terms.

